# 4294967297 fits `long` but exceeds RtInt's range, in Clipping's far-plane
# float slot. GMANRIBTokenize::parseNum rejects an out-of-range integer
# literal with RIE_RANGE regardless of the destination it is headed for --
# an integer literal is bounded against RtInt at the token, before the
# parser ever learns whether it wants an RtInt or an RtFloat. Without that
# token-level bound, nextFloat's LONGINT branch would carry no RtInt bound
# of its own, so this exact literal would silently become the float
# 4294967297.0 instead of raising an error.
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 4294967297
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
